---
// THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO "LIVE GRAPH OFFLINE" STRIP HERE.
//
// The handoff specifies one above this bar, with two dashed cards explaining
// that the mini-map is "hidden, not broken" and that search "falls back to a
// plain form post to /search". Neither is true of what shipped: the mini-map
// keeps its build-time neighbourhood and stays correct, and search reads a
// static index from the CDN and never touches the API at all (ADR-0003).
//
// So the strip would announce a degradation the reader does not have, and its
// explanations would describe behaviour the site does not exhibit — the exact
// defect #111, #114 and #53 exist to remove, in the surface meant to reassure.
// Every write that genuinely fails says so where it failed instead, and /t is
// the one route with real offline copy because it is the one route that
// actually needs the API. Revisit this if a surface ever degrades silently.
import SearchPanel from './SearchPanel';
import TrailCount from './TrailCount';
// The count is read from localStorage after hydration, so it is no longer
// something a page can be asked to know. It was a prop, and every page passed
// either nothing or the length of a hardcoded one-element array (#114).
---
<header class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-line px-[26px] py-3.5">
  <a href="/" class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold text-starlight no-underline">
    the<span class="text-thread">∞</span>.ai
  </a>
  <nav class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <SearchPanel client:idle mode="overlay" />
    <a href="/concepts" class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.12em] text-dust no-underline hover:text-starlight">
      Concepts
    </a>
    <TrailCount client:idle />
  </nav>
</header>
